<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pope Gregory XI</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1329–1378</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Pierre Roger de Beaufort</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gregory XI was pope from 1370 to 1378, the last French pope. Urged by Catherine of Siena among others, he moved the papal court from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avignon">Avignon</a> back to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in 1377 to restore papal authority in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the Papal States. His death the next year was followed by the disputed election that began the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-schism">Great Western Schism</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-xi.jpg" alt="Pope Gregory XI" width="252" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Virgil Master and his atelier · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Duke_of_Anjou_leading_Pope_Gregory_XI_to_the_palace_at_Avignon,_while_cardinals_follow_(cropped).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
